        "subheading": "<p>Autism evaluations are designed to provide diagnostic clarity when there are questions about social communication, sensory differences, restricted or repetitive patterns of behavior, emotional regulation, executive functioning, developmental history, or differences in how a person experiences and responds to the world. </p><p>At Center for Balanced Living, autism evaluations are completed with clinical care, developmental context, and respect for the whole person. </p><p>The goal is not to reduce someone to a label, but to better understand patterns of functioning, clarify diagnosis when appropriate, and provide recommendations that support daily life, treatment planning, school supports, workplace needs, and self-understanding.</p>",
